1
00:00:00,064 --> 00:00:01,566
This Tesla can jump.

2
00:00:01,567 --> 00:00:02,446
But rocket thrust

3
00:00:02,447 --> 00:00:03,781
comes with a catch.

4
00:00:03,782 --> 00:00:04,701
These jets blast

5
00:00:04,702 --> 00:00:05,992
compressed air.

6
00:00:05,993 --> 00:00:06,672
Every burst

7
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:07,775
uses some up.

8
00:00:07,776 --> 00:00:08,775
Keeping a car airborne

9
00:00:08,776 --> 00:00:10,055
on thrust means pushing

10
00:00:10,056 --> 00:00:11,581
against its entire weight.

11
00:00:11,582 --> 00:00:12,141
Bigger tanks

12
00:00:12,142 --> 00:00:13,181
can buy more time,

13
00:00:13,182 --> 00:00:13,981
but add weight

14
00:00:13,982 --> 00:00:15,316
and need protection.

15
00:00:15,317 --> 00:00:16,811
Then comes balance.

16
00:00:16,812 --> 00:00:17,611
Thrust that misses

17
00:00:17,612 --> 00:00:18,491
the center of mass

18
00:00:18,492 --> 00:00:19,607
can make it rotate.

19
00:00:19,608 --> 00:00:20,247
Other thrusters

20
00:00:20,248 --> 00:00:21,047
can correct that,

21
00:00:21,048 --> 00:00:22,007
but those corrections

22
00:00:22,008 --> 00:00:23,294
use air too.

23
00:00:23,324 --> 00:00:24,123
And fire a jet

24
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:25,238
near loose gravel?

25
00:00:25,239 --> 00:00:25,878
That blast

26
00:00:25,879 --> 00:00:27,780
can send debris flying.

27
00:00:27,781 --> 00:00:28,380
None of this

28
00:00:28,381 --> 00:00:29,309
breaks physics.

29
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:30,509
It gives a sports car

30
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:31,945
spacecraft problems.

31
00:00:31,946 --> 00:00:33,065
Full Roadster breakdown

32
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:34,263
in the linked video.
